  "question": {
    "text": "Consider a triangular plot <math><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math> with sides <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo></math> <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;A vertical lamp-post at the mid-point <math><mi>D</mi></math> of <math><mi>A</mi><mi>C</mi></math> subtends an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> at <math><mi>B</mi><mo>.</mo></math> The height (in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math>) of the lamp-post is:",
    "image": null
  },
